.TH garuda-toolbox-kernels 1  "garuda-toolbox 6.3.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox\-kernels \- List, install and remove kernels and their headers
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox kernels\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
List, install and remove kernels and their headers
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-kernels\-list(1)
List the kernels: installed, running, available
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-kernels\-install(1)
Install a kernel. It is used after the next restart
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-kernels\-remove(1)
Remove an installed kernel. The running one stays
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-kernels\-headers(1)
Install the headers of an installed kernel, for DKMS modules
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-kernels\-default(1)
Boot an installed kernel by default, through the boot menu
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  garuda\-toolbox kernels list \-\-json
  garuda\-toolbox kernels install linux\-lts
.SH "SEE ALSO"
garuda\-toolbox(1)
